WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.416
(audience applauding)
- All right, y'all!

00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:03.062
Welcome to the season two premiere

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:05.432
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show!"

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:06.488
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.488 --> 00:00:08.880
Give it up for America's dad, Bob Saget!

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.870
Thank you so much, Bob.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.280
- I love you, Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.109
- I love you, Bob Saget.

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:16.020
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.285
I love him so much.

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:18.330
He's awesome.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.630
The last time I was on this
stage was over six months ago,

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.950
and a lot has changed, for
you, for me, for all of us.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.170
Let's just get this out of the way.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.340
2020 has been a dumpster fire.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.020
Yep, just all the word I
can't say on this show,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.320
just piled together, and it's on fire.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.730
That's really what it feels like.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.440
So, from day one,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.350
I did, though, say that this show

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.920
was going to be about connection,

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.340
and not even 2020 and
socially distancing ourselves

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.500
and all the hurdles are going
to get in the way of that.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.550
We are still going to stay connected,

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.890
and I wanted to sing
those classic TV songs

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.070
because in hard times
when we're separated,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:02.010
it's the nostalgic moments
with families and friends

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.660
that hold us together.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.510
And, well, you've just
been stuck with them,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:07.242
if you wanted to or not.

00:01:07.242 --> 00:01:08.320
(laughs)

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.210
Plus, we've all been
on lockdown, you know,

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.550
with nothing else to do but
really binge watch the old shows

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.680
'cause we're out of all the new ones,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.810
'cause nobody can tape anything.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:16.790
It's fine.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.623
(audience laughing)

00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:19.300
So give it up for my band, y'all!

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.694
They're back!

00:01:20.694 --> 00:01:23.249
(audience cheering)

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.499
Looking so fly.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.230
We are all back together,
band, crew, all of us!

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.780
And we are here in our studio, finally.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.100
We've really been looking forward to this.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.730
I know everyone is in their
own worlds with their jobs,

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.470
but a big thank you to my TV
friends who join us today.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:41.496
Ed Asner from "The Mary Tyler Moore Show!"

00:01:41.496 --> 00:01:42.329
(audience cheering)

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:45.190
George Wendt and John
Ratzenberger from "Cheers!"

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.817
And David Coulier and Jodie
Sweetin from "Full House!"

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.240
Thank you guys so much.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.073
And as you can see,

00:01:52.073 --> 00:01:55.050
we have a new kind of
audience as well this season.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.502
These are actually our
brand new house seats

00:01:57.502 --> 00:02:00.030
filled with people from
all over the country.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.120
For example, we have Leah dialing in

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.770
from her home in Columbus, Ohio.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.690
Wave, Leah, what's up!

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:07.090
Oh, I love the color red.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.410
Wear a great color, yes.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.650
All right, and over there is Eleanor

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.300
from Raleigh, North Carolina.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.030
Give it up. Come on, Eleanor!

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.103
Give us a wave!

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.100
All right, well this is
all thanks to our partners

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.470
at The Video Call Center.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.880
We're actually the first to use

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.710
their new crowd view
technology, which is super cool.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.420
That means any of you watching from home

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.410
can actually use your
cell phone or your laptop

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.530
and be in our audience,

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.630
which is actually kind of cool.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.130
We're leaning into how we're
navigating the new way.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.270
But just head to kellyclarksonshow.com

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.540
to find out how you can be a part

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.520
of this fun, fantastic
moment that we're having.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.250
I'm so glad I can still connect

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.320
with all of you, though, in my studio

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.410
because as you probably know,

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.070
2020 has brought a lot of
change also to my personal life.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.450
Definitely didn't see
anything coming that came.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.760
But what I'm dealing with is hard

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.210
because it involves
more than just my heart.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.660
It involves a lot of little hearts.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.000
You know, we have four kids,
and divorce is never easy,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.160
and we're both from divorced families,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.790
so, you know, we know the
best thing here is to protect

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.340
our children and their little hearts.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.760
So I'm usually very open,

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.500
and I usually talk about everything,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.920
but in this case I will talk
a little bit here and there

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.200
about how it affects me personally,

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.020
but probably won't go too far into it

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.120
because, you know, I'm a mama bear,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.100
and my kids come first.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.440
Although I do love you all.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.273
But I am okay.

00:03:24.273 --> 00:03:26.400
Everybody keeps asking, "Are
you okay? Are you okay?"

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.550
And I am! The answer is yes.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.020
It's one of those things that
it's okay 'cause it matters.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.020
It was something important.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.690
And I know a lot of you
at home, unfortunately,

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.530
have probably been through it,

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.220
either as a kid or just as yourself

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.190
in your own relationships.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.580
So, I feel you,

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.290
and it is a bad connection
to have with people,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.579
but I will say this though,

00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:47.760
when I got upset when I was a kid,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.870
I had a problem saying how I felt,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.670
and my mom told me to start writing.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.080
And that's actually how
I get my feelings out.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.630
So I probably won't
speak about it too much,

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.510
but you definitely will hear it.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.563
Musically, probably.

00:03:58.563 --> 00:04:00.750
That's how I became a song writer.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.240
Music's always been my outlet

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.700
to help me get through difficult times.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.620
And this year, I've been
listening to a lot of music,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.770
and I've also been writing
a lot of music as well.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.530
So, this week we decided
to dedicate to music.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.110
It's dedicated to musicians,

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.310
and it's dedicated to the
way music heals all of us.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:21.250
And we've got a lineup of
unforgettable performances

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.470
you won't want to miss.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.770
And I've been told there
are some surprises,

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.060
even if I don't know about them.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.440
Very excited.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.940
Although surprises make
me nervous, but it's fine.

